    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="1318" n="1160" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1160"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gummeré to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-06-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 9, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 91.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In further confirmation of my No. 90, of
                    May 31, 1906, reporting the murder of May 27 of Mr. A. Charbonnier, a French
                    citizen, I have the honor to report that two French cruisers of the first class,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Jeanne d’Arc</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kléber</hi>, and the third-class cruiser <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Galilée</hi> have arrived at Tangier to support the French minister in his
                    endeavors to secure the apprehension and punishment of the murderers, and in
                    such other demands as he may make to the Moorish Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. R. Gummeeé.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
